1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,984
The discussion lasted until midnight.

2
00:00:01,984 --> 00:00:11,428
Some members wanted to lend the map to the council; many wanted to keep it private; a few wanted to stop altogether.

3
00:00:11,428 --> 00:00:15,403
“Every option has a price,” Lin said.

4
00:00:15,403 --> 00:00:25,997
“No option is free.” He sat with his eye on the hole in the tent where the rain came through, and nobody could describe the shape of the decision.

5
00:00:25,997 --> 00:00:32,356
There were a number of gates still untested, though the room was warm.

6
00:00:32,356 --> 00:00:36,566
Each member wrote one sentence on a piece of paper.

7
00:00:36,566 --> 00:00:39,351
Most of them were unusable.

8
00:00:39,351 --> 00:00:48,280
There were several commas, one plural mistake, and a remark from a tutor about the ultimate purpose of the project.

9
00:00:48,280 --> 00:01:01,223
“A single arbitrary rule,” Maya said, “is worse than no rule at all.” She had quite enough of niceties, and which of them had the patience left to argue?

10
00:01:01,223 --> 00:01:08,353
“Write the next page for me,” she added, “and keep it to one sentence.”

11
00:01:08,353 --> 00:01:13,347
The confrontation came in a seminar on dynamic systems.

12
00:01:13,347 --> 00:01:22,926
A guest lecturer in golf trousers and a bright sleeve described how an army of small decisions can cover a million small failures.

13
00:01:22,926 --> 00:01:29,220
“You cannot bless a plan into working,” he said with an excess of confidence.

14
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:43,489
“You have to test it.” His umbrella, a parcel of notes, a necklace of coffee stains on the napkin, and a hamburger eaten in three bites made him a highly unlikely authority.

15
00:01:43,489 --> 00:01:50,693
The seminar turned into a tutorial on how quickly a good idea can become a habit.

16
00:01:50,693 --> 00:02:01,957
The team chose the least dramatic path: multiple small trials, one per gate, with the results of each published beside the respective gate.

17
00:02:01,957 --> 00:02:07,271
The lesson was simple and the several commas of the first draft were gone.

18
00:02:07,271 --> 00:02:18,550
The extreme option, a single official map, would fail; the ultimate one, no map at all, would fail worse.

19
00:02:18,550 --> 00:02:24,420
They met again in the city office, where the report was finally accepted.

20
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:45,113
“Again,” the guy from the city desk said, “you have done something small and honest.” Her answer was a smile and one sentence: “That is the whole unit of progress.” It was not a quality they could measure, but it was property they could defend, and that was the point.

21
00:02:45,113 --> 00:02:50,431
Every member of the team signed the last page.
